  "strategy": "1. Approach and rationale:\nThe proposed approach integrates scalable optimization with specialized repair operators to escape local minima. Key innovations include:\n   - Hybrid dimensionality reduction using gradient thresholds (not penalty multipliers)\n   - Variable selection based on gradient information gradients_norm / (sum_gradients_\u00b11)\n   - Progressive repair with exponential tightening of repair targets\n   - Co-evolution of parent and shadow candidates in multi-threaded optimization\n\nThe method systematically balances expansion at boundaries and smoothing near the mean, avoiding the grid-lock in standard local searches. The central idea is to maintain population diversity while focusing computation on promising regions.\n\n2. Mathematical specification:\nProblem: Minimize F(h) = max_k \u222bh(x)(1-h(x+k))dx\ns.t. \u222bh(x)dx = 1 [0\u2264h(x)\u22641]\n\nDiscretization:\n- h \u2208 \u211d^n n = number of samples\n- dx = 2/n\n- C5 = max_k (integral) * n/2\n\nObjective: F(h) = (1/n) * norm(correlation(h, 1-h, mode='full'))_\u221e\n\nRepair projection:\n_proj_sum(h, target): Bisection method\nlo = -\u03b5_hi = \u03b4\nfor i=1 to 50:\n  mid = (lo+hi)/2\n  find s = E[min(max>]h(x)-mid, bounds) close to target\n\nConstraint handling: Variable projection preserves continuity\n\n3. Implementation procedure:\ndef run(seed=42, budget_s=1100, n_initial=560):\n  \n  # Initialization\n  rng = RandomState(seed)\n  h0 = np.array(initial_h_values)\n  h0_repaired = _repair(h0)\n  \n  def elapsed():\n      return time.time() - start_time\n  def is_out_of_budget():\n      return elapsed() > budget_s\n\n  n = len(h0_repaired)\n  dx = 2.0/n\n\n  candidates = [h0_repaired]\n  best = None\n  best_c5 = float('inf')\n\n  # Phase 1: Local diversification\n  for i in range(5):\n      # Create variant\n      variant = _create_variation(candidates)\n      candidates.append(variant)\n  \n  # Phase 2: Parallel optimization\n  threads = []\n  n_workers = min(cpu_count(), len(candidates))\n  budget_per = (budget_s - 10) / n_workers\n  for h in candidates:\n      t = Thread(target=lambda h=h, budget=budget_per: _optimize_thread(h, budget))\n      threads.append(t)\n      t.start()\n\n  # Phase 3: Gradient-enhanced repair\n  for h in candidates:\n      grad = _gradient(h)\n      _oproxy(h, grad)   # Progressive repair\n\n  # Phase 4: Selection\n  for thread in threads:\n      thread.join()\n  \n  best = min(candidates, key=lambda h: _eval(h))\n\n  return (best, _eval(best), n)\n\ndef _gradient(h):\n  # Central differences + analytic gradient components\n\ndef _create_variation(h):\n  # Amplitude = 0.2 * rng.randn()\n  # Shift = 10 * rng.randn()\n  return _repair(h + amplitude * np.sin(shift * grid))\n\ndef _oproxy(h, grad):\n  decay = 0.997\n  for i=0.1 to 0.1% of dimensions:\n      select i based on gradient[i] / (average_gradient_\u00b11 + 1e-9)\n      adjust h[i] by grad[i] * random factor\n\n4. Search choices:\n- Variations: 5 per batch\n- Budget allocation: 90% to gradient refinement, 10% to new variants\n- Repair patience: 50 iterations max\n- Projection: Bisection method\n- Dimensionality: n/4 max threads per worker\n\n5. Compute budget:\n- Estimate: 500 seconds wall-clock\n- Monitor likelihood of improvement based on gradient curvature\n- Early termination if no improvement >5 consecutive iterations\n- Progressive tightening of integral target during repair\n\n6. Validation and return:\n  - Apply _eval(best)\n  - Clip bounds to [0,1]\n  - Verify integral sum == n/2\n  - Return (h, C5_value, n)\n\nChecks: \n  assert 0.9 < h.min() < h.max() < 1.1\n  assert abs(sum(h) - n/2) < 1e-5\n\nFallback: O(5) fallback structure if time elapses",
